From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:13:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Keep dGPU power state on S3 resume

With ACPI runtime PM the OS may power the dGPU off before entering S3.
Romstage still applies the "enable_dual_graphics" option on resume
and turns the GPU back on behind the back of the OS.

Leave the dGPU power state alone on S3 resume when runtime PM is
enabled. The power resource _STA reports the actual state, so the OS
powers the GPU on again when it needs it.

TEST=Built for W541 and T440p. Not tested on hardware yet.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c
index 518bd4b61..64d8cd442 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include <option.h>
 #include <ec/lenovo/pmh7/pmh7.h>
 #include <device/pci_ops.h>
+#include <romstage_handoff.h>
 
 void mainboard_config_rcba(void)
 {
@@ -23,10 +24,20 @@ void mb_late_romstage_setup(void)
 {
 	u8 enable_peg = get_uint_option("enable_dual_graphics", 0);
 
-	bool power_en = pmh7_dgpu_power_state();
+	/*
+	 * With ACPI runtime PM the OS may have powered the dGPU off before
+	 * suspending: keep that state on S3 resume, the power resource _STA
+	 * reports it and the OS powers the GPU back on when it needs it.
+	 */
+	bool keep_state = CONFIG(LENOVO_HASWELL_DGPU_RUNTIME_PM) && enable_peg &&
+			  romstage_handoff_is_resume();
 
-	if (enable_peg != power_en)
-		pmh7_dgpu_power_enable(!power_en);
+	if (!keep_state) {
+		bool power_en = pmh7_dgpu_power_state();
+
+		if (enable_peg != power_en)
+			pmh7_dgpu_power_enable(!power_en);
+	}
 
 	if (!enable_peg) {
 		// Hide disabled dGPU device
-- 
